{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>The way of the wilderness, Sea of Reeds.</b> The way of the wilderness of the Sea of Reeds. Like 'the Ark of the Covenant,' which means the ark that is the Ark of the Covenant; and likewise 'the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil,' which means the tree that is knowledge of good and evil." "<b>And chamushim.</b> What Rashi explained as 'armed' — to tell you that it was not because they feared the Egyptians that He turned them by way of the Sea of Reeds, since the Israelites went up from Egypt armed; and furthermore, so that you not wonder whence they had weapons for the war in the wilderness and the wars in the Land of Israel. Another interpretation: <b>and chamushim</b> — from the language of 'and he provisioned the land of Egypt,' meaning provisioned with the dough they took out of Egypt, which sufficed for them until the fifteenth of Iyyar, because He turned them by way of the wilderness."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:40.439310967Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}